%% Sequence Diagram 1 — Interconnected "skill-learned" Cascade (the USP)
%% Chapter 4/5: shows agents cooperating via shared memory, never calling each other directly
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant FE as React Frontend
    participant LR as Learning Router<br/>(FastAPI)
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>(shared memory)
    participant EV as agent_events<br/>(event bus)
    participant M2 as Model 2<br/>Skill Extractor
    participant GA as Skill Gap Agent
    participant RA as Resume Architect

    U->>FE: Mark skill "Docker" as learned
    FE->>LR: POST /learning/complete
    LR->>DB: UPDATE skills (proficiency, source='learning')
    LR->>EV: INSERT event {type: skill_learned, payload: Docker}
    LR-->>FE: 200 OK (UI not blocked)
    FE-->>U: ✅ Skill saved instantly

    Note over EV,RA: Background cascade (< 30 s)
    EV->>GA: skill_learned event consumed
    GA->>M2: re-extract skills for open analyses
    M2-->>GA: present / missing skills
    GA->>DB: UPDATE gap_analyses (Docker → present, status refreshed)
    GA->>DB: UPDATE learning_plans (progress recalculated)
    EV->>RA: same event consumed
    RA->>DB: UPDATE resumes SET needs_refresh = true
    Note over U,DB: Next visit: fresh gap report + "resume refresh" flag
